course: dictionary
lesson: 15898
title: Unlit: dark or not burning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unlit is made of two parts: un- means not, and lit is the past of light. So unlit means not lit: no light is on, or nothing is burning. «The unlit path was hard to find at night.» The words at night and hard to find are clues that the path had no lights, so it was dark.
explain: Unlit has a second meaning. «She picked up an unlit candle from the shelf.» The candle was not on fire. You can check by swapping in your meaning: an unlit candle is a candle that is not burning, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Unlit can be important for safety. An unlit road is dark, so drivers and walkers may not see you. That is why you should wear bright or reflective clothes on an unlit path and carry a torch.
fact: Unlit means not having lights switched on, so it is dark.
fact: Unlit can also mean not set on fire or not burning, as in «an unlit candle».
fact: The opposite of unlit is lit, as in «a lit lamp».
fact: «An unlit road» is dangerous at night, so bright clothes and lights keep you safe.
fact: «Unlit» is made of un- (not) and lit (the past of light).
exercise: «The unlit street was silent and dark.» What does unlit mean here? | *Not having lights on | Full of bright shop windows | Very noisy | Newly painted
exercise: What does unlit mean in «an unlit candle»? | Made of wax that smells nice | *Not set on fire or burning | Very tall and thin | Bright and shiny
exercise: Why should cyclists have lights on an unlit road? | So they can sing as they ride | *So drivers can see them | So the bike is heavier | So they can go faster
test: What should you wear on an unlit path at night? | *Bright or reflective clothes | Dark black clothes so you can hide | Your pyjamas | A large hat
test: «The unlit house looked spooky.» Why does unlit make the house feel spooky? | Because it has a new roof | Because it is painted bright yellow | Because it is full of music | *Because it is dark with no lights on
exam: Which phrase describes a candle that is not burning? | Bright and tall | A lit lamp | A hot cup of cocoa | *An unlit candle
